[node name="RatColonyFollowers" type="Node2D" unique_id=1757510028 node_paths=PackedStringArray("followers")]
process_mode = 3
editor_description = "Persistent mining colony activated after Rotini's second encounter. Assign Follow Target to the production MinerRig when instanced. The fixed pool below is the whole colony: rank, tint, draw order and slot position are derived at runtime, so moving an authored pool child changes nothing. Web lights a smaller even slice of the same pool.

The formation is rebuilt from the player outward on both sides, with 132px of protected center clearance. All thirty-two actors use the normal-size individual mouse art; no clump drawing is used. Four staggered depth ranks share the miner's ground face while overlap, shadows and lighting fill the floor. Every visible mouse swings on every successful player hit and removes terrain at its own pickaxe-contact frame.

The 2.5D read comes from draw-order recession, shader depth haze and directional light, overlapping silhouettes, and a soft actor_ground_shadow.gdshader contact under each mouse. Every rank keeps the same ground baseline and large readable size; depth does not turn mice into floating miniatures.

The same MiningController swing preparation and swing signals start the miner and every mouse at the same playback multiplier. Each contact opens a narrow tunnel at that mouse's pickaxe from the miner's authoritative start row through the full depth of that hit, without granting duplicate rewards. Thirty-two individual tunnels are batched into one renderer publication. One back mouse hops after recovering from every second impact.

Target preference alternates left and right through Caspian's public set_preferred_side API. Reset sends zero, cancels every pending action and terrain contact, and hides the whole fixed pool.

Draw order puts the front rank on the SECOND layer - z 1, between terrain strata 0 and 1 - which is exactly where MinerRig.buried_draw_order stands the miner while he is mining. That is the directive for every character: the colony digs beside him, so it is layered as he is, and the foreground rock closes over them together. It used to sit at z 2, level with the frontmost stratum, which drew the nearest rats in front of the rock the miner is buried in. Each rank behind the front recedes one stratum.

These four numbers only mean anything against TerrainLayerProfile.layer_z_indices, currently (2, 0, -1, -2), and nothing ties the two together. Renumber the strata and the colony silently changes which rock it is in front of."
script = ExtResource("1_followers")
followers = [NodePath("Formation/Rat00"), NodePath("Formation/Rat01"), NodePath("Formation/Rat02"), NodePath("Formation/Rat03"), NodePath("Formation/Rat04"), NodePath("Formation/Rat05"), NodePath("Formation/Rat06"), NodePath("Formation/Rat07"), NodePath("Formation/Rat08"), NodePath("Formation/Rat09"), NodePath("Formation/Rat10"), NodePath("Formation/Rat11"), NodePath("Formation/Rat12"), NodePath("Formation/Rat13"), NodePath("Formation/Rat14"), NodePath("Formation/Rat15"), NodePath("Formation/Rat16"), NodePath("Formation/Rat17"), NodePath("Formation/Rat18"), NodePath("Formation/Rat19"), NodePath("Formation/Rat20"), NodePath("Formation/Rat21"), NodePath("Formation/Rat22"), NodePath("Formation/Rat23"), NodePath("Formation/Rat24"), NodePath("Formation/Rat25"), NodePath("Formation/Rat26"), NodePath("Formation/Rat27"), NodePath("Formation/Rat28"), NodePath("Formation/Rat29"), NodePath("Formation/Rat30"), NodePath("Formation/Rat31")]
